#X text 215 83 A model obtained by a suitable five-mode truncation
of the Navier-Stokes equations for a two-dimensional incompressible
fluid on a torus:;
#X text 215 138 dx1= -2*x1 + 4*x2*x3 + 4*x4*x5;
#X text 215 163 dx2= -9*x2 + 3*x1*x3;
#X text 215 188 dx3= -5*x3 - 7*x1*x2 + reyn;
#X text 215 213 dx4= -5*x4 - x1*x5;
#X text 215 238 dx5= -x5 - 3*x1*x4;
#X text 215 263 ---;
#X text 215 288 Where <reyn> is the Reynolds number \, and exibits
an interesting variety of different behaviors for different ranges
of <reyn>. For the critical values of <reyn> \, the most interesting
feature is the stochastic behavior observed when R1 < <reyn> < R2\.
With 28.73 < R1 > 29.0 and R2 ± = 33.43\.;
